================================================================================
Bundled third-party content
================================================================================

Two directories in this repository are snapshots of other projects, copied in on
2026-08-13 so that work on rampscan has the demand-side dataset and the founding
arguments in reach. They are redistributed here, so they are named here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/context/ramprules/  —  the FedRAMP Rules Hub dataset
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Source:   ramprules — https://ramprules.com
  Snapshot: dataset version 2026.07.14.01, taken 2026-08-13
  Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
            https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
            upstream text: data/LICENSE in github.com/snymrova/ramprules.com

  Attribution, in the form the upstream licence asks for:

      "FedRAMP Rules Hub dataset (ramprules.com), CC BY 4.0"
      dataset_version 2026.07.14.01

`derived/` is a copy of ramprules' published JSON slices — the KSI graph, the
control set, the AWS evidence recipes and the automation frontier. rampscan
reads it in dev mode and 17 test files depend on it, which is why it is shipped
whole rather than trimmed or fetched. **The CC BY 4.0 grant covers `derived/`
and nothing else here**, because upstream scoped its licence to the data
directories and said so explicitly: Creative Commons licences are not intended
for software, and the code around that dataset is deliberately left ungranted.

Five files sit beside `derived/` in this directory and are NOT covered by that
grant — `README.md`, `PRODUCT.md`, `DATASET-FACTS.md` and the two type
declarations `types.ts` and `raw-types.ts`, all copied from outside upstream's
licensed data directories. They are here as reading material for a person or an
agent working on rampscan; nothing in this repository imports or tests against
them, and they carry no licence. They come from the same author as this
repository, so there is no third-party permission at stake — but a reader who
reuses this snapshot should carry `derived/` and leave those five, because they
are the ones the grant does not reach.

It is a snapshot and it rots. rampscan pins against `dataset_version` and, per
slice, against `overlay_version` — never against these copies. The source of
truth is upstream, and `docs/context/README.md` says how to check a fact against
it.

Where this repository's own adjudication records cite or disagree with an
upstream disposition, the citation is recorded in the record itself
(`citesUpstream`), not here.

