================================================================================
Third-party tools rampscan invokes but does not redistribute
================================================================================

No copy of any of these ships in this repository. rampscan resolves each one at
run time — a binary already on your PATH is used as-is, otherwise the pinned
container image is run — and it never installs anything on the host. Each tool
reaches you from its own publisher, under its own licence, which travels with the
binary or image you obtained. They are named here because rampscan's output cites
their findings, and a reader deserves to know whose analysis they are reading.

  syft         1.51.0     anchore/syft:v1.51.0                   SBOM
  grype        0.117.0    anchore/grype:v0.117.0                 container advisories
  gitleaks     8.24.3     ghcr.io/gitleaks/gitleaks:v8.24.3      secrets in history
  osv-scanner  2.5.0      ghcr.io/google/osv-scanner:v2.5.0      dependency advisories
  semgrep      1.173.0    semgrep/semgrep:1.173.0                static analysis
  checkov      3.3.11     bridgecrew/checkov:3.3.11              IaC misconfiguration
  spectral     6.16.3     stoplight/spectral:6.16.3              API description linting

The authoritative list is packages/collectors/tools.json; this table is a copy of
it and the file wins.

PocketBase (pinned 0.39.10) backs the local console. Its binary is likewise not
vendored here — `pnpm fetch-pocketbase` downloads it from the official release and
verifies it against the sha256 sums pinned in console/pocketbase/version.json.

npm dependencies are declared in the package manifests and resolved by pnpm from
the registry. None is vendored into this repository.
